DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iissbbllaannkk() and iissbbllaannkk__ll() functions test for a space or tab charac‐
     ter.  For any locale, this includes the following standard characters:

     “\t”    “ ”

     In the "C" locale, a successful iissbbllaannkk() or iissbbllaannkk__ll() test is limited
     to these characters only.  The value of the argument must be repre‐
     sentable as an _u_n_s_i_g_n_e_d _c_h_a_r or the value of EOF.

     The iissbbllaannkk__ll() function takes an explicit locale argument, whereas the
     iissbbllaannkk() function uses the current global or per-thread locale.

